{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656082",
      "title": "Understanding View Encapsulation",
      "lectureOrder": 395,
      "videoOrder": 365,
      "sourceHash": "ca9b033ba0601e99d9b6c7d2ae6d5d0052c4bc36657104b014c79c88e33de2ff",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.4,
          "end": 3.95,
          "en": "-: I'm not sure if you noticed it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.95,
          "end": 7.47,
          "en": "in the last lectures, with our working application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.47,
          "end": 10.803,
          "en": "if I add Servers or blueprints, something changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.079,
          "end": 14.61,
          "en": "A new Server down here in the blueprint",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.61,
          "end": 16.8,
          "en": "as well as the paragraph right at the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.8,
          "end": 19.56,
          "en": "no longer has a blue color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.56,
          "end": 22.92,
          "en": "Now, it was colored blue before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.92,
          "end": 25.92,
          "en": "because in the app.component.css file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.92,
          "end": 30.42,
          "en": "we defined that paragraphs should have a blue text color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.42,
          "end": 33.24,
          "en": "But both paragraphs were moved.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.24,
          "end": 36.3,
          "en": "They are no longer part of our app.component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.3,
          "end": 39.6,
          "en": "The first paragraph is part of the cockpit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.6,
          "end": 41.01,
          "en": "and the second paragraph, well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.01,
          "end": 43.68,
          "en": "that is inside of our Server element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.68,
          "end": 45.27,
          "en": "But isn't that strange?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.27,
          "end": 50.27,
          "en": "Here on this CSS definition, we just say paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.97,
          "end": 54.57,
          "en": "so it should affect all paragraphs in our whole app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.57,
          "end": 56.28,
          "en": "Now, you might say, \"Well, no,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.28,
          "end": 58.29,
          "en": "it's in the app.components.css file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.29,
          "end": 62.52,
          "en": "so clearly it only belongs to this template.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.52,
          "end": 67.23,
          "en": "But is that so clear, because the way CSS works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.23,
          "end": 69.87,
          "en": "it doesn't really care in which CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.87,
          "end": 73.2,
          "en": "you define a rule, it simply is applied",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.2,
          "end": 76.17,
          "en": "to the whole document, normally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.17,
          "end": 80.4,
          "en": "So this actually is a behavior enforced by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.4,
          "end": 83.85,
          "en": "which is not the default behavior of the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.85,
          "end": 86.88,
          "en": "So while of course these CSS files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.88,
          "end": 90.33,
          "en": "have the goal of encapsulating styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.33,
          "end": 93.63,
          "en": "for the component they belong to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.63,
          "end": 96.21000000000001,
          "en": "this, again, is not a default behavior,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.21000000000001,
          "end": 98.03999999999999,
          "en": "Angular gives us this behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.03999999999999,
          "end": 100.56,
          "en": "It's a great behavior because, with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.56,
          "end": 103.38,
          "en": "we can make sure that whichever styles we define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.38,
          "end": 106.11,
          "en": "in a CSS file will only get applied",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.11,
          "end": 108.21000000000001,
          "en": "to the component they belong to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.21000000000001,
          "end": 111.45,
          "en": "However, here, of course, this means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.45,
          "end": 116.28,
          "en": "that now we would have to copy this blue color here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.28,
          "end": 121.28,
          "en": "to all our other components that we want to use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.65,
          "end": 124.68,
          "en": "Well, I never wanted to use it on the cockpit anyways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.68,
          "end": 127.47,
          "en": "but I will copy it to the server element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.47,
          "end": 130.14,
          "en": "and if we now change this and let it reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.14,
          "end": 133.02,
          "en": "and enter something here and add a new blueprint,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.02,
          "end": 135.093,
          "en": "now you see this is blue again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.96,
          "end": 139.5,
          "en": "Now, it's interesting if we inspect this text here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.5,
          "end": 143.13,
          "en": "in the developer tools, you see that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.13,
          "end": 144.87,
          "en": "if you look at the styles, clearly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.87,
          "end": 148.95,
          "en": "here we assign the blue color, but do you see that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.95,
          "end": 153.95,
          "en": "The selector changed, before, we had just P here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.02,
          "end": 156.96,
          "en": "just paragraph, now it's paragraph and then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.96,
          "end": 161.96,
          "en": "this very strange attribute, _ngcontent- ejo-2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.12,
          "end": 167.973,
          "en": "Well, I don't know about you, but I didn't add it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.84,
          "end": 172.26,
          "en": "You can see this attribute here on the paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.26,
          "end": 174.48,
          "en": "That is why the style gets applied here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.48,
          "end": 177.03,
          "en": "because this style definition says",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.03,
          "end": 180.48,
          "en": "make every text blue which is in a paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.48,
          "end": 182.7,
          "en": "where the paragraph has this attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 182.7,
          "end": 184.44,
          "en": "Something which is true for the paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 184.44,
          "end": 186.213,
          "en": "holding this specific text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 187.05,
          "end": 190.65,
          "en": "Now, the other paragraph we have in app-cockpit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 190.65,
          "end": 193.74,
          "en": "here in the div, this paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 193.74,
          "end": 196.96,
          "en": "does have a different attribute, _ngcontent-ejo1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 199.11,
          "end": 202.62,
          "en": "Down here, we have ejo-2, that is why the styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 202.62,
          "end": 204.9,
          "en": "gets not applied to this paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 204.9,
          "end": 207.36,
          "en": "And all these strange attributes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 207.36,
          "end": 210.51,
          "en": "which you can see all over the place here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.51,
          "end": 213.27,
          "en": "all these strange attributes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 213.27,
          "end": 218.27,
          "en": "are applied to their specific elements by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 219.32999999999998,
          "end": 224.32999999999998,
          "en": "Angular, as I told you, enforces this style encapsulation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 224.55,
          "end": 226.89,
          "en": "And it can't do that magically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.89,
          "end": 231.54,
          "en": "so the way it does it is it simply gives the same attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 231.54,
          "end": 234.42000000000002,
          "en": "to all elements in a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 234.42000000000002,
          "end": 236.43,
          "en": "So all elements in this cockpit component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 236.43,
          "end": 239.733,
          "en": "have ngcontent_ejo-1 attached to it, as you can see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 240.78,
          "end": 242.61,
          "en": "And it does this for each component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 242.61,
          "end": 245.43,
          "en": "with different unique attribute names,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 245.43,
          "end": 250.08,
          "en": "ejo-1 and ejo-0 and ejo-2,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 250.08,
          "end": 253.8,
          "en": "and with that, it can make sure that, once it changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 253.8,
          "end": 256.14,
          "en": "your style selector, it automatically adds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 256.14,
          "end": 258.33,
          "en": "this attribute selector to all your styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 258.33,
          "end": 261.21,
          "en": "defined for a component, that these styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 261.21,
          "end": 265.71,
          "en": "get only applied to elements of that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 265.71,
          "end": 268.59,
          "en": "This is how it enforces this behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 268.59,
          "end": 272.19,
          "en": "It kind of emulates the shadow dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 272.19,
          "end": 275.85,
          "en": "The shadow dom is a technology not supported by all browsers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 275.85,
          "end": 280.85,
          "en": "where each element has its kind of own shadow dom behind it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 281.7,
          "end": 285.75,
          "en": "where you then could assign styles to each element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 285.75,
          "end": 289.95,
          "en": "but as this technology is not supported by all browsers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 289.95,
          "end": 292.40999999999997,
          "en": "this is how Angular emulates it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 292.40999999999997,
          "end": 294.57,
          "en": "and that is the default behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 294.57,
          "end": 297.573,
          "en": "of view encapsulation in Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
